{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/con/skills/pulls/26","id":4851833288,"node_id":"PR_kwDORUy0bs8AAAABITEZyA","html_url":"https://github.com/con/skills/pull/26","diff_url":"https://github.com/con/skills/pull/26.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/con/skills/pull/26.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/con/skills/issues/26","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/con/skills/pulls/26/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/con/skills/pulls/26/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/con/skills/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/con/skills/issues/26/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/con/skills/statuses/664d48bafca7e05d942707713bd896f95932b3a4","number":26,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"STAMPED skills: implementation","user":{"login":"yarikoptic-gitmate","id":41385986,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxMzg1OTg2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41385986?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yarikoptic-gitmate","html_url":"https://github.com/yarikoptic-gitmate","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yarikoptic-gitmate/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yarikoptic-gitmate/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yarikoptic-gitmate/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yarikoptic-gitmate/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yarikoptic-gitmate/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yarikoptic-gitmate/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yarikoptic-gitmate/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yarikoptic-gitmate/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yarikoptic-gitmate/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"ATM just implementation and measure phase 1\n\n## What this is\n\nAn implementation of the STAMPED skills plan from #24, branched from the same\nbase (`ea48c88`) and taken through phase 1 with the numbers it was measured at.\nIt is deliberately a **competing** PR: #24 has since recorded five decisions\nthat the implementation found reason to disagree with, and\n[`docs/stamped/divergence.md`](docs/stamped/divergence.md) argues each one from\na run rather than a preference — while adopting the eight things #24 got right.\n\nAddresses stamped-principles/stamped-agent-skills#3.\n\n## What it adds\n\n**Two skills**\n\n- `stamped-conventions` 0.2.0 (not user-invocable) — the checklist pinned at\n  0.3.1 (vendored from `stamped-checklist-schema@v0.3.1` with a lock recording\n  tag, commit and sha256), the five-status verdict vocabulary, the response and\n  report format, project kinds, the DataLad stack reference, and two scripts:\n  `vendor_checklist.py` (the only writer of the pin; `--check` verifies it) and\n  `encode_response.py` (the only writer of a checklist-app URL, and the decoder\n  that turns a checklist a human filled in the web app into reference answers).\n- `assess-alignment-with-stamped-principles` 0.2.0 — read-only by contract,\n  with 13 probes that answer 13 of the 17 MUST items, 3 SHOULD items and\n  may/001 from committed state, plus `fresh_rerun.py` for the one check that\n  has to leave the host. 180 lines of instructions, under the budget the skill\n  declares and CI enforces.\n\n**An eval harness, outside the skills** (`evals/stamped/`)\n\n- a known-good R0 fixture built with plain git — no datalad, no network;\n- **15 scripted mutants**, one injected defect each, two of them negative\n  controls that assert an item must *not* move;\n- **6 judgement mutants** — prose defects no probe can see, graded by a blind\n  subagent, with a gate that refuses any mutant whose defect trips a probe;\n- `blind_run.py`, `judgement_calibrate.py`, `calibrate.py`, `run.py`,\n  `grade.py`, `aggregate.py`;\n- the R0 use case with exact column definitions, a deterministic selection\n  rule, and a science oracle;\n- `gold/` (a reference answer for a real object) and `blind-runs/` (what five\n  independent subagents returned, as they returned it).\n\n**CI** — `tox -e validate` gains E007 (a skill's own `max-lines` budget) and\nW004 (prose repeated between a skill's files), and scans bundled Python\nrecursively; `tox -e stamped-evals` runs 38 tests and the mutant calibration on\nevery change.\n\n**Ready to file elsewhere** (`docs/stamped/upstream/`) — a `ChecklistResponse`\nLinkML schema for stamped-checklist-schema, lint-clean and validated against a\nreal 31-item response, an app-exported payload and an example; and a\npaper-vs-schema drift issue whose every claim is verified with line numbers,\nincluding two checklist items that are the same sentence.\n\n## What it measured\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| Scripted mutants detected | **15/15**, no collateral item flips |\n| False `unmet`/`partial` on the clean fixture | **0/17** answered items |\n| Probe sweep on a 1265-commit object | **3.6 s**, and it finds the `url = ../..` gap |\n| Blind subagent runs | **5** (3× sonnet, 1× haiku, 1 control) |\n| Judgement mutants detected | **4/4** run, two then *retired* because a probe can do it |\n| Agreement, independent run vs reference | **30/31** items after the fixes |\n| Tests | **38** |\n\nFive blind runs cost ≈750 k tokens, which is the number to plan iterations\nagainst.\n\n## What the runs changed\n\nThe development rule in `AGENTS.md` is new and repo-wide: **every non-trivial\nchange to a skill is tested by handing it to a fresh, blind subagent with a\nconcrete scope**, which returns its work product *and* the places the\ninstructions failed it. The authoring session walking through its own procedure\nproves nothing.\n\nThat paid immediately. The runs found, among others: a probe that knew `/home`\nand `/tmp` but not `/data/<user>`, so two entry points pinned to one machine\nread as clean; `must/005` applying a size criterion the item does not state;\n`should/003` answered from a property it does not ask about; `13/13 probes met`\non an object whose documented install was Homebrew-only; a fixture whose run\nrecords named an image it never created; and — from the control run on the\n*unmutated* object — that the fixture's input was pinned to a commit the real\nds007116 answers with `upload-pack: not our ref`, and that its own remote 404s.\nEach became a fix **plus** a regression artifact; 16 friction items were\nreported, 15 acted on, one disproved.\n\n## Checks\n\n```console\ntox -e validate        # 0 errors\ntox -e stamped-evals   # 38 passed, mutants 15/15, false unmet 0/17\n```\n\n`docs/stamped/` has no `allowed-tools`/naming conflict with #23 today, but if\n#23 merges first this branch renames its assessor to `assess-stamped` rather\nthan shipping two — see divergence.md §5.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_014yrjCucFpBst3yix1SYaZm\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-14T01:53:35Z","updated_at":"2026-10-14T15:45:26Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"e1ae5b76742352b0fd224138df0921311ee1629c","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"con:stamped-skills-impl","ref":"stamped-skills-impl","repo":{"id":1162654830,"node_id":"R_kgDORUy0bg","name":"skills","full_name":"con/skills","owner":{"login":"con","id":13295221,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjEzMjk1MjIx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13295221?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/con","html_url":"https://github.com/con","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/con/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/con/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/con/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/con/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url"